# 3D Web Design Rules

## Version pairing

- `@react-three/fiber@9.x` requires React 19 (`>=19 <19.4`) and `three >=0.156`.
- Do not mix R3F 8 with React 19 or R3F 9 with React 18.
- Import `Canvas`, `useFrame`, `useThree` from `@react-three/fiber`.

## Scene brief

- One hero scene only: "Signal Core" - a polished low-poly form with a thin orbital ring and a few fragments representing vision plus AI agents.
- One meaningful interaction: pointer/touch rotates or focuses the core; keyboard-accessible DOM control mirrors the effect.
- The scene is decorative atmosphere, never the only place information exists.
- No external GLTF, HDR environment, texture, or font downloads in v1. Use procedural geometry and lights.

## GPU budget

- Draw calls: target < 30, hard ceiling < 50.
- Triangles: target < 50k, hard ceiling < 100k.
- One canvas per page. Never render a second canvas in a modal or footer.
- `dpr={[1, 1.5]}`, `frameloop="demand"` where the scene can rest, and `performance={{ min: 0.5 }}`.
- No shadows, post-processing, transmission, refraction, or real-time reflections.
- Reuse geometries/materials; dispose on unmount; never allocate in `useFrame`.
- Prefer `meshStandardMaterial`/`meshPhysicalMaterial` with simple lights.
- Target 45+ fps on a mid-tier laptop and 30+ fps on a low-tier phone; degrade before dropping frames.

## Loading and fallbacks

- The hero headline must be the LCP element, not the canvas.
- Load the 3D chunk after the main content using `next/dynamic` with `ssr: false` and idle/intersection scheduling.
- Skip 3D and show the static poster when any of these is true:
  - `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`
  - `navigator.connection.saveData`
  - `deviceMemory <= 4` or `hardwareConcurrency <= 4` (treat as heuristic)
  - WebGL context creation fails
  - the device reports a software renderer
- Poster fallback must be a real designed composition (SVG/CSS), not a grey box.
- Pause rendering when offscreen or when the document is hidden; cancel observers/listeners on unmount.
- Handle `webglcontextlost` gracefully by switching to the poster.

## Accessibility

- Canvas is `aria-hidden="true"` when purely atmospheric.
- If it has an interaction, provide a visible DOM button with an explicit label and equivalent outcome.
- Do not put readable text, project names, or CTAs inside the canvas.
- Provide a text description of the scene near the canvas for screen-reader users.
- Honor reduced motion by freezing the scene; do not merely slow it down.

## Anti-patterns

- A full-screen WebGL background that blocks text selection or scroll.
- Heavy orbit controls on mobile.
- Continuous rendering while idle.
- Loading three.js on every route or for every user.
- Using 3D to compensate for weak layout/typography.
- Dragging the whole page into a 3D interaction without a keyboard alternative.

## Verification

- Check the Network panel: the 3D chunk must not load on reduced-motion or save-data.
- Check `renderer.info.render.calls` and `triangles` in development.
- Run a 30-second idle test: no sustained CPU/GPU work.
- Navigate away and back: no leaked animation frames, listeners, or WebGL contexts.

